as traumatized fans of Game of Thrones  know all too well lady Catelyn Stark was  shockingly and brutally slain in the  penultimate episode of season 3 but with  the show's final season about to arrive  fans are once again wondering could she  somehow still be alive on the surface it  sounds impossible after all the infamous  red wedding scene couldn't have been  more clear about the deaths of Catelyn  her new daughter-in-law to Lisa and her  son Robb Stark the erstwhile King in the  north  after being betrayed by Lord Roose  Bolton and Lord Walder Frey who had been  secretly conspiring with the villainous  House Lannister to destroy the Starks  Robb Tulisa and Catelyn were all stabbed  to death in horribly graphic fashion  there's no doubt about it  she was very definitely dead but is she  going to stay dead look who know so much  yeah well it just so happens that your  friend here is only mostly dead there's  a big difference between mostly dead and  all that first it's important to  remember that people come back from the  dead in Game of Thrones all the time  both Jon Snow and beric Dondarrion have  done it thanks to the kiss of life from  the fire-god known as the Lord of Light  and then on the slightly less happy side  of things the night king has been  resurrecting the dead for eons forming a  zombie army that includes not just  giants but a giant dragon  so it's theoretically possible that  Catelyn could be brought back but more  importantly it's actually already  happened in the books that is author  george RR martin who wrote the fantasy  novels that form the basis for Game of  Thrones resurrected Catelyn not long  after the red wedding with beric  Dondarrion surrendering his own  immortality in order to return Catelyn  to the land of the living as the  vengeful Lady Stoneheart for her part  actress Michelle Fairley told  Entertainment Weekly that Catelyn would  not be returning regardless of what  happened in the books  yeah the characters dead she's dead you  respect the writers decision I knew the  arc and that was it  they can't stick to the books 100% it's  impossible they only have 10 hours per  season they have got to keep it dramatic  and exciting and extraneous stuff along  the way gets lost in order to maintain  the quality of a brilliant show still  people associated with Game of Thrones  have been known to lie in the past in  order to prevent spoilers most famously  for example the folks at HBO swore up  and down for  year that Jon Snow was actually really  dead for good after being betrayed at  the end of season five naturally of  course he was back on his feet in season  six plus even some of the show stars  have publicly hinted that more major  characters will also be brought back  from the grave on the side of the night  king in 2017 Nikolaj coster-waldau who  plays Jamie Lannister told Esquire the  beer is that I would be turned into one  of those undead that would suck you know  some of the main characters are going to  get turned they are going to be some  blue-eyed main characters running around  and god I hope it's not me some fans  though think that Catelyn has already  reappeared as Lady Stoneheart in season  seven passing through the background of  a scene at Winterfell at the same moment  her daughter Arya mentioned her you  swore to serve both my mothers don't is  didn't you and others believe that the  first season eight trailer which shows  the stark children gathering in the  family crypt hints at catlins return  all because I couldn't love a motherless  but it still seems pretty unlikely that  Catelyn will ever return don't worry  though  Game of Thrones has plenty of big fish  to fry dangling plot threads to tie up  and mysteries to solve in its final six  episodes so even if cat never makes a  surprise return viewers will still have  plenty of juicy storylines to sink their  teeth into when season 8 premieres on  HBO on Sunday April 14 check out one of  our newest videos right here plus even  more looper videos about Game of Thrones  are coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

